// The first-person view: rotate_y(-yaw) * translate(-camx,-eye,-camz), the
// standard "undo the camera's own transform" camera matrix (composed via
// gl_mat_mul, which applies its second/right argument first -- see
// backends/gl/gl.h). Split into rot.id/trans.id because the seven native
// calls it takes don't fit one block's 3-action budget.
//
// build_proj rebuilds the perspective matrix from the window's LIVE aspect
// ratio every frame (gl_aspect_x1000()) so a resize never stretches the
// image (backends/gl/README.md's "Window resize" section).

build_view() {
  int rot = view_rot();
  int trans = view_trans();
  int view_matrix = gl_mat_mul(rot, trans);
} return int view_matrix;
given create_player ():(2)
given create_player ():(2) then build_view:(5)

build_projection() {
  int aspect_ratio = gl_aspect_x1000();
  int projection_matrix = gl_mat_perspective(70000, aspect_ratio, 100, 20000);
} return int projection_matrix;
